  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be a cubic function such that <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mn>1</mn> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>″</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mn>2</mn> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0.</mn></mrow> </math> If <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is a point of local maxima of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the local minimum value of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> occurs at",
    "image": null
  },
